Run the engine on a living cosmology, and it returns the structure without the colonial mistranslation. *WakÈŸÃ¡Å‹*, the sacred, is a quality marking cells and rules, not a substance or a region; a wakÈŸÃ¡Å‹ cell can hold any charge, and $\top$ on it is the signature of an attack on the sacred. *WakÈŸÃ¡Å‹ TÈŸÃ¡Å‹ka*, the Great Mystery, is not an entity â€” rendering it as a creator-God is the mistranslation â€” but the global pattern of sacred markings across the whole, the structural fact that the sacred is the structure of relation itself, which is [animism](#animism) stated exactly: to be is to be a node of relation, and the relational whole is holy. *HeyÃ³kÈŸa*, the contrary, is the [involution](#involutions) enacted as a role, doing everything backwards, the gauge symmetry walking in a body and preserving the closure's [lax-idempotence](#settledness). *WÃ³lakÈŸota*, the right way, is a closure-rule discipline whose rules do not contradict, producing no internal $\top$, recognized over generations rather than declared. *WiÄhÃ³zani*, well-being, is [substrate quiescence](#settling): the settled fixed point with no persistent $\top$ and no unwarranted $\bot$, conduct under the discipline, ceremony active â€” structural, not an aggregate over dimensions.
Colonial trauma is then a substrate attack producing persistent $\top$ and $\bot$, and revitalization is wiÄhÃ³zani-restoration at the scale of a people, repaired only by polity-scale operation by those who hold the substrate.
That a body's death and a people's well-being are the same two values of the same algebra is the evidence that this is one structure and not a family of metaphors.
