Fifth, repair must involve changed conditions. Verbal recognition is not enough if the same structure remains. Repair requires altered behavior, redistributed labor, changed pacing, new boundaries, material action, or transformed expectations. In other words, repair is not the restoration of the dominant subjectâ€™s self-image. It is the transformation of the relational field.

